// Runs #96 (45800651582, 14m36s), #97 (45801208075, 12m58s) and
// #98 (45801390708, 14m34s) fix - all three FAILED at Soong
// ninja-file generation on the SAME fix code (the #93 fix HELD:
// prune step + pre-build guard passed in all three), but with
// THREE different error sets on one commit (the subset-reporting
// lesson at its extreme, again). Run #96's set is the widest;
// the fix below covers the UNION of all three runs' errors, so
// the next run is not left to rediscover the other runs' subsets.
// Verified live (LineageOS lineage-22.2 / AOSP android-15.0.0_r32
// unless noted): every module below is in an unsynced project
// and is never built for this HAL-only target, so only the NAMES
// have to exist for Soong's parse. Types match each module's
// real type and how its referencers use it (see the per-stub
// notes). Public visibility on purpose: the referencers live
// in other packages.
//
// android_stubs_current / android_test_stubs_current /
// android_system_stubs_current - the SDK stubs Soong resolves
// sdk_version "current" / "test_current" / "system_current" to
// (same family as the already-stubbed
// android_module_lib_stubs_current, runs #87/#88/#89, which
// HELD - #98 reports no error for it). Referencers: the
// java_sdk_library-generated .stubs.from-source modules of
// test_framework-apexd / test_service-apexd, libtombstone_proto_java
// (sdk_version "current"), libaconfig_java_proto_lite/nano
// (sdk_version "current"), aconfig_storage_file.test.java /
// aconfig_storage_read_unit (sdk_version "test_current") and the
// auto-generated RRO characteristics modules. Empty java_library
// stubs, exactly like the #62/#64 ART stubs.
//
// sysprop-library-stub-platform - the stub library Soong's
// sysprop_library codegen (build/soong/sysprop/sysprop_library.go,
// AOSP r32, verified live) puts in `libs:` of every generated
// java_library for a platform-owned sysprop_library (the <name>
// java lib has Sdk_version "core_current" and Libs
// [javaSyspropStub]; the <name>_public stub is created the same
// way). Referencers: com.android.sysprop.apex_public,
// charger_sysprop_public, LibGuiProperties_public,
// SurfaceFlingerProperties_public. Empty java_library stub.
//
// ext + framework - the framework java_library modules
// (frameworks/base/Android.bp at AOSP r32: `framework` line 561
// and `ext` line 638, both java_library). Referencers: the
// java_sdk_library-generated .stubs.source / .impl modules of
// test_framework-apexd / test_service-apexd (their impl compiles
// against the full framework), libsimpleparcelable_java,
// aidl_test_java_* (system/tools/aidl), backported_fixes_proto
// and the frameworks/native opengl/binder test apps. Empty
// java_library stubs. (The .source vs .from-source naming differs
// between runs #96/#97 and #98 - the floating LineageOS pins
// moved build/soong between their syncs - so BOTH the stubs
// family (this block) and the ext/framework pair are needed.)
//
// androidx.test.runner + androidx.test.core - java_library in
// external/androidx (unsynced). Referencers: the aconfig_storage_*
// android_test modules and the aidl_test_java_* modules
// (static_libs:). Empty java_library stubs.
//
// framework-res + org.lineageos.platform-res - the resource
// packages the auto-generated RRO product modules overlay:
// framework-res is an android_app in frameworks/base/core/res/
// Android.bp (verified live: sdk_version "core_platform",
// certificate "platform"); org.lineageos.platform-res is the
// LineageOS platform resources package (vendor/lineage,
// unsynced). Referencers: the AppInRebootlessApex /
// PrivAppInRebootlessApex / TestLatency
// __auto_generated_rro_product modules (and the aconfig_storage_*
// android_test modules). Stubbed as android_app with a dummy
// manifest (package "android" / "org.lineageos.platform",
// yuzora-stubs/AndroidManifest.xml /
// AndroidManifest-lineage.xml, created below) + Empty.java,
// sdk_version "none", system_modules "none",
// use_resource_processor false (mirrors the real framework-res;
// no res/ dir is needed). NOT pruned: the RROs' source apps
// live in the kept apexs_testdata file, which the kept
// system/apex/apexd/Android.bp references (its ApexTestCases
// data lists name the test apexes) - same reason as run #58.
//
// libz / libgrpc++ / libusb / libusb_platform / libcrypto /
// libstatssocket - cc_library_shared, all used in shared_libs:
// by a synced module (libjsoncpp was in this list until the
// runs #105/#106/#107 fix - see its note below - it is now a
// plain cc_library stub): libz by liblibz_sys
// (rust_library, external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/libz-sys);
// libgrpc++ by libgrpcio_sys (same tree, crates/grpcio-sys);
// libusb + libusb_platform by liblibusb1_sys /
// liblibusb1_sys_platform (crates/libusb1-sys; the real ones are
// cc_library in external/libusb, verified live at r32);
// libjsoncpp by aidl_metadata_parser + hidl_metadata_parser
// (cc_binary, shared_libs, verified live at r32). Runs
// #105/#106/#107 fix: run #105 ALSO reports libjsoncpp as a
// missing STATIC variant (libprocessgroup_proto_test,
// system/core/libprocessgroup/profiles/Android.bp:108,
// static_libs) - upstream libjsoncpp is plain cc_library
// (external/jsoncpp/Android.bp, verified live at r32), which
// builds BOTH variants, so the stub below changes from
// cc_library_shared to plain cc_library (same fix as the
// #99/#100/#101 protobuf stubs). The shared_libs users above
// are unaffected - a plain cc_library still provides the
// shared variant.
// libcrypto by libcrypto_utils (cc_library, shared_libs,
// verified live at lineage-22.2); libstatssocket by
// libstatslog_express (cc_library, shared_libs - the module is
// defined nowhere in the synced tree: system/core/libstats has
// only socket_lazy at r32/lineage-22.2). Empty cc_library_shared
// stubs with empty.c, host_supported + windows (same form as
// the #84 libsqlite stub). Runs #99/#100/#101 fix: the #96
// round wrote this comment but never created the
// libstatssocket stub block - run #101 reports it undefined
// (system/core/libstats/expresslog/Android.bp:76). Stub added
// below.
//
// libprotobuf-cpp-lite / libprotobuf-cpp-full - the C++
// protobuf runtimes (external/protobuf, NOT synced - verified
// in run #82: no external/protobuf entry in the manifest).
// Referencers: the cc_library_static proto modules
// (libtombstone_proto, lib_apex_manifest_proto_lite,
// lib_apex_blocklist_proto, libvintf_proto,
// libaconfig_storage_protos_cc, lib_linker_config_proto_lite,
// ota_metadata_proto_cc need -lite; cc_analyzer_proto,
// lib_apex_manifest_proto, lib_apex_session_state_proto,
// libprocessgroup_proto need -full), all via static_libs:.
// Runs #99/#100/#101 fix - the #96 round stubbed these as
// cc_library_static, but upstream both are plain cc_library
// (verified live at r32: external/protobuf/Android.bp,
// host_supported, min_sdk_version "29"), which builds BOTH
// the static and the shared variant. Run #101 reports
// "missing variant os:linux_glibc,arch:x86_64,link:shared
// (only static available)" for both - a consumer needs the
// shared variant, which a cc_library_static stub can never
// provide. Changed to plain cc_library stubs with empty.c,
// host_supported + windows. (Upstream disables the static
// variant of -full on device, but a cc_library stub still
// satisfies every name reference; consumers link -full via
// shared_libs upstream.)
//
// libjemalloc5_je_prefixed - cc_library_static in
// external/jemalloc (unsynced), used in static_libs: by the
// rust_library_host libtikv_jemalloc_sys
// (crates/tikv-jemalloc-sys). Empty cc_library_static stub.
//
// libhardware_headers - cc_library_headers in
// hardware/libhardware (unsynced), used in header_libs: by
// hwvulkan_headers (frameworks/native/vulkan, cc_library_headers).
// Empty cc_library_headers stub (same form as the #84
// libchrome-gestures_headers stub).
//
// gwp_asan_headers - cc_library_headers for GWP-ASan
// (external/gwp-asan, unsynced), used in header_libs: by
// libc_native_allocator_defaults (bionic/libc/Android.bp - the
// MAIN libc defaults, not a test) and by bionic_tests_defaults.
// Empty cc_library_headers stub. (Pruning bionic/tests would NOT
// fix this: the libc defaults still need it.)
//
// dex2oatd - art_cc_binary in art/dex2oat (unsynced; verified
// live at r32: `art_cc_binary { name: "dex2oatd", ... }`, the
// binary dexpreopt depends on). Referencers: the
// java_sdk_library-generated .impl modules of
// test_framework-apexd / test_service-apexd. art_cc_binary is a
// cc_binary subclass and art/ is not synced, so stub as
// cc_binary with empty.c, host_supported, device_supported NOT
// set to false (BOTH variants, same form as the #87 linkerconfig
// stub - dexpreopt needs the host binary and the device variant
// must exist too).
//
// libcxx - the Rust cxx crate (external/rust/crates/cxx,
// unsynced; NOT vendored in android-crates-io - the r32
// crates/ listing has 389 entries and no cxx). Referencer:
// libmoveit (rust_library_host, crates/moveit) via rustlibs:.
// Empty rust_library stub (crate_name "cxx", srcs lib.rs,
// created below - an empty file is a valid empty crate),
// host_supported (libmoveit is host-only).
java_library {
    name: "android_stubs_current",
    srcs: ["Empty.java"],
    sdk_version: "none",
    system_modules: "none",
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
