// Runs #102/#103/#104 fix: "sdk_public_34_system_modules" -
// the ONLY runtime Soong error in all three runs (raw-log
// verbatim, identical in #102/#103/#104):
//   error: frameworks/native/libs/binder/ndk/tests/Android.bp:132:1:
//   "IBinderVendorDoubleLoadTest-java" depends on undefined module
//   "sdk_public_34_system_modules".
// Root cause, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 / AOSP r32:
// IBinderVendorDoubleLoadTest is an aidl_interface (that file,
// lines 254-268: unstable, vendor) with the Java backend enabled
// (no `backend: { java: { enabled: false } }`), so Soong
// generates the IBinderVendorDoubleLoadTest-java java_library
// with a NUMERIC sdk_version 34. Soong's decodeSdkDep
// (build/soong/java/sdk.go) gives every java module with a
// numeric sdk_version above 29 an implicit system_modules dep
// `sdk_<kind>_<ver>_system_modules` (Java 9+ uses system
// modules; 29 and below is Java 8 and gets none - which is why
// sdk-29 AppInRebootlessApex never needed one). Upstream that
// module is a java_system_modules_import generated by the
// `prebuilt_apis` "sdk" module in prebuilts/sdk/Android.bp
// (one per scope+version, only for core-for-system-modules.jar;
// build/soong/java/prebuilt_apis.go, createSystemModules) -
// prebuilts/sdk is NOT synced, so no sdk_*_system_modules
// exists in this tree. The #96 fix stubbed the other half of
// the dep (android_stubs_current, the bootclasspath lib); now
// the system-modules half surfaces - the same one-layer-deeper
// pattern as runs #30/#33/#75. The 46 other "error:" lines in
// the Build step are the runner echoing the step script itself
// (the ::error:: pre-build-guard echo commands that did not
// fire), NOT build errors.
// Fix, same established pattern (stub, don't sync): this stub
// IS a java_system_modules - the dep's type (a java_library
// stub would fail Soong's type check; same reason as the #75
// core-all-system-modules stub). Its libs list holds our own
// empty android_stubs_current stub (defined above) so the list
// is non-empty and always resolves. The sibling
// sdk_module-lib_34_system_modules is stubbed too:
// decodeSdkDep's systemModuleKind maps system/test/core kinds
// to public and system-server to module, so for ver 34 only
// the public and the module-lib names can ever be referenced -
// that is the complete layer, not just the reported subset.
// (No synced module uses sdk_version module_34 today - its
// jar would have errored first - but the stub costs nothing
// and the subset-reporting lesson says the next run is the
// arbiter.) NOT java_system_modules_import: its deps mutator
// prefixes lib names with `prebuilt_`, which would create a
// new undefined-module error.
java_system_modules {
    name: "sdk_public_34_system_modules",
    libs: ["android_stubs_current"],
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
java_system_modules {
    name: "sdk_module-lib_34_system_modules",
    libs: ["android_module_lib_stubs_current"],
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #105/#106/#107 fix: the #102/#103/#104 fix HELD in
// all three (prune step + pre-build guard passed). The three
// runs report THREE different error sets on the same fix code
// (subset-reporting at its extreme, again): #105 (28 lines)
// the widest, #106 (4), #107 (2). The fix covers the UNION
// (30 lines). Raw-log verbatim, per run:
//   #107 (45819014190, 13m58s, manual, f8e598c) - 2 lines,
//   both build/make/tools/aconfig/aconfig/Android.bp:105:1
//   ("aconfig.test.java"): androidx.test.rules, testng.
//   #106 (45818868390, 14m41s, auto, f8e598c) - 4 lines:
//   system/tools/aidl/Android.bp:857:1 + :841:1
//   (aidl_test_java_service_permission,
//   aidl_test_java_client_permission):
//   frameworks-base-testutils; frameworks/native/headers/
//   Android.bp:11:1 (media_plugin_headers):
//   libstagefright_headers, libstagefright_foundation_headers.
//   #105 (45818724942, 15m25s, auto, fab59cc) - 28 lines:
//   both media_plugin_headers lines + both aconfig.test.java
//   lines + pyfakefs x4 (build/soong/bloaty/Android.bp:19,
//   build/make/ci/Android.bp:52, :20, :74) + asuite_cc_client
//   x3 (build/make/tools/edit_monitor/Android.bp:33,
//   build/make/tools/tool_event_logger/Android.bp:33, :46) +
//   watchdog (edit_monitor:33) + the libgralloctypes triple
//   (frameworks/native/libs/gralloc/types/Android.bp:58:30
//   export_shared_lib_headers V6-ndk, :25:1 mapper@4.0,
//   :25:1 libhidlbase) + libssl x4 / libcrypto_static x2
//   (external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/quiche/Android.bp)
//   + libgoogle-benchmark x2 / libtinyxml2 x2 (bionic tests +
//   benchmarks) + libgtest_isolated (bionic/tests:855) +
//   libprocinfo (bionic/tests:809) + the libprocessgroup
//   triple (system/core/libprocessgroup/profiles/Android.bp:108:
//   libjsoncpp missing STATIC variant, libjsonpbverify,
//   libjsonpbparse). (The 46 other "error:" lines in each Build
// step are the runner echoing the step script itself, NOT build
// errors. NOTE: the first UI-log read of #107 reported the
// aconfig error path as frameworks/base/aconfig/test/Android.bp
// - WRONG; the raw log says build/make/tools/aconfig/aconfig/
// Android.bp, and frameworks/base has no aconfig/ dir at
// lineage-22.2 (verified by git ls-tree) and is not synced.)
// Root causes, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 /
// AOSP android-15.0.0_r32 (each stub's type is its upstream
// type, or the type the referencer's property requires where
// the home was not traced to a file):
// - androidx.test.rules + testng: static_libs of the
//   android_test aconfig.test.java (build/make/tools/aconfig/
//   aconfig/Android.bp:105, lineage-22.2). testng is
//   java_library in external/testng (r32, host_supported);
//   androidx.test.rules is java_library in external/androidx,
//   same family as the #96 androidx.test.runner/core stubs.
// - frameworks-base-testutils: static_libs of the java_test
//   aidl_test_java_client_permission / _service_permission
//   (system/tools/aidl/Android.bp:841, :857, r32) - java_library
//   in unsynced frameworks/base (defining file not traced).
// - libstagefright_headers + libstagefright_foundation_headers:
//   header_libs (+ export_header_lib_headers) of the
//   cc_library_headers media_plugin_headers
//   (frameworks/native/headers/Android.bp:11, lineage-22.2).
//   libstagefright_headers is cc_library_headers in
//   frameworks/av media/libstagefright/Android.bp
//   (lineage-22.2); _foundation_headers is cc_library_headers
//   in frameworks/av (unsynced; the defining file was not
//   located - no media/libstagefright/foundation/ dir in the
//   lineage-22.2 or r32 frameworks/av checkouts).
// - pyfakefs: libs: of python_test_host bloaty_merger_test
//   (build/soong/bloaty/Android.bp:19) + build_test_suites_*
//   (build/make/ci/Android.bp) - python_library in
//   external/python/pyfakefs/pyfakefs/Android.bp (r32,
//   host_supported).
// - asuite_cc_client + watchdog: libs: of python_library_host
//   edit_monitor_lib (build/make/tools/edit_monitor/Android.bp:
//   33, lineage-22.2) and python_binary_host tool_event_logger
//   (+ _test). watchdog is python_library_host in
//   external/python/watchdog/src/watchdog/Android.bp (r32);
//   asuite_cc_client is a python library (home not traced to
//   a file) - both stubbed with srcs empty.py, same form as
//   the #99 python stubs.
// - libssl + libcrypto_static: libquiche (rust_library,
//   shared_libs) + libquiche_ffi (rust_ffi, static_libs) +
//   libquiche_static (rust_library_rlib, static_libs)
//   (external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/quiche/Android.bp,
//   r32). Upstream external/boringssl: libssl is plain
//   cc_library, libcrypto_static is cc_library_static (r32).
//   libssl is used in BOTH shared_libs and static_libs, so
//   only a plain cc_library stub satisfies both; libcrypto
//   (shared_libs) is already stubbed as cc_library_shared.
// - libgoogle-benchmark: static_libs of cc_library_static
//   libbionic_spawn_benchmark (bionic/benchmarks/spawn/
//   Android.bp:53) + the cc_benchmark_host
//   bionic-benchmarks-glibc (no such entry in its own .bp text
//   or its bionic-benchmarks-defaults - Soong's cc_benchmark
//   type adds the benchmark runtime implicitly). Upstream
//   cc_library_static in external/google-benchmark (r32).
// - libtinyxml2: static_libs of libBionicStandardTests +
//   bionic-benchmarks-defaults (bionic/benchmarks/Android.bp)
//   - plain cc_library in external/tinyxml2 (r32,
//   host_supported).
// - libgtest_isolated: static_libs of libBionicStandardTests
//   + whole_static_libs of libBionicCtsGtestMain
//   (bionic/tests/Android.bp:369, :855, lineage-22.2) - NOT
//   defined in external/googletest at r32 (all four .bp files
//   checked); home not traced - plain cc_library stub (the
//   static variant is what both referencers need).
// - libprocinfo: static_libs of cc_test_library
//   libBionicLoaderTests (bionic/tests/Android.bp:809,
//   lineage-22.2) - NOT in system/core at lineage-22.2 or
//   r32 (no libprocinfo dir in either checkout) and NOT in
//   bionic; home not traced - plain cc_library stub.
// - libjsonpbverify + libjsonpbparse: static_libs of
//   cc_test_host libprocessgroup_proto_test (system/core/
//   libprocessgroup/profiles/Android.bp:108, lineage-22.2) -
//   NOT in system/core/libprocessgroup/Android.bp at r32;
//   home not traced - plain cc_library stubs.
// - libjsoncpp missing variant (same file:108): the #96 stub
//   is cc_library_shared, but the test needs the STATIC
//   variant ("missing variant os:linux_glibc,arch:x86_64,
//   link:static"). Upstream libjsoncpp is plain cc_library
//   (external/jsoncpp/Android.bp, r32) - the stub changes to
//   plain cc_library, same fix as the #99/#100/#101 protobuf
//   stubs. Its shared_libs users (aidl/hidl metadata parsers)
//   are unaffected.
// - android.hardware.graphics.common-V6-ndk +
//   android.hardware.graphics.mapper@4.0 + libhidlbase:
//   libgralloctypes (cc_library, frameworks/native/libs/
//   gralloc/types/Android.bp, lineage-22.2) lists mapper@4.0
//   + libhidlbase in shared_libs and V6-ndk + mapper@4.0 +
//   libhidlbase in export_shared_lib_headers. mapper@4.0 is a
//   hidl_interface in hardware/interfaces/graphics/mapper/4.0
//   and V6-ndk is the NDK lib of the aidl_interface
//   android.hardware.graphics.common (frozen: false, aidl_api
//   1-5 + current = V6) - BOTH dirs are deleted by the closure
//   prune below (hardware/interfaces keeps ONLY light/aidl +
//   compatibility_matrices + common/aidl + input), so neither
//   module exists in this tree. libhidlbase is plain
//   cc_library in system/libhidl (r32, unsynced). V6-ndk +
//   mapper@4.0 stubbed as cc_library_shared (the HIDL/AIDL
//   generated libs are shared); libhidlbase as plain
//   cc_library (its upstream type). AND the
//   android.hardware.graphics.common-ndk_shared cc_defaults
//   stub (runs #48/#49/#50) gains shared_libs V6-ndk: the real
//   generated defaults forwards the -ndk lib into shared_libs,
//   and the empty stub is what makes Soong report V6-ndk as
//   "not in shared_libs" on the export check.
java_library {
    name: "androidx.test.rules",
    srcs: ["Empty.java"],
    sdk_version: "none",
    system_modules: "none",
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
