// Runs #111/#112/#113 fix: the #110 fix HELD in all three
// (prune step passed in 1s + pre-build guard passed). All
// three fail at Soong ninja generation, ~36-55s into the
// build step, on the SAME fix code (head bfbbfcb - the #110
// fix, workflow fd7e33e). Subset-reporting again: #113 and
// #112 report the same pair, #111 reports a different one.
// The fix covers the UNION (3 lines). Raw-log verbatim:
//   #113 (45835491023, 14m40s, manual, bfbbfcb) + #112
//   (45835366346, 14m30s, auto, bfbbfcb) - 2 lines each:
//   system/core/fs_mgr/libdm/Android.bp:22:1 libdm depends
//   on undefined module libext2_uuid; system/core/fs_mgr/
//   libfstab/Android.bp:24:1 libfstab depends on undefined
//   module libgsi_headers.
//   #111 (45835194480, 15m01s, auto, e000389) - 1 line:
//   external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/drm-ffi/
//   Android.bp:16:1 libdrm_ffi depends on undefined module
//   libdrm_sys.
//   (The 50 other error: lines in each Build step are the
//   runner echoing the pre-build-guard echo commands that
//   did NOT fire - the guard printed Pre-build guard passed
//   in all three runs.)
// Root causes, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 /
// AOSP android-15.0.0_r32:
// - libext2_uuid: static_libs of the cc_library_static
//   libdm (system/core/fs_mgr/libdm/Android.bp,
//   lineage-22.2). Upstream plain cc_library in
//   external/e2fsprogs/lib/uuid/Android.bp (lineage-22.2,
//   host_supported) - external/e2fsprogs is NOT synced (not
//   in the 32-project manifest). Stubbed as plain cc_library
//   (covers the static_libs use, same as the libssl /
//   libjsoncpp pattern).
// - libgsi_headers: header_libs of the cc_library_static
//   libfstab (system/core/fs_mgr/libfstab/Android.bp,
//   lineage-22.2). Upstream cc_library_headers in
//   platform/system/gsid/Android.bp (r32, host_supported,
//   export_include_dirs include) - system/gsid is its own
//   project, NOT synced; system/core never contained it (no
//   libgsi dir under fs_mgr at lineage-22.2). Stubbed as
//   cc_library_headers, mirroring the #105
//   libstagefright_headers stub.
// - libgsi + libgsid: NOT reported by any run yet, but the
//   same unsynced gsid file defines them (libgsi cc_library,
//   libgsid cc_library_static) and the SYNCED
//   system/core/fs_mgr/Android.bp references both in
//   static_libs (libfs_mgr_defaults lists libgsi; remount
//   lists libgsid) - they are the next subset-reporting
//   layer, so both are stubbed now (plain cc_library covers
//   the static use; same complete-layer precedent as the
//   #102 sibling sdk_module-lib_34_system_modules stub).
// - libdrm_sys: rustlibs of the rust_library libdrm_ffi
//   (external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/drm-ffi/
//   Android.bp, r32, crate drm_ffi 0.8.0). NO defining file
//   exists at r32 or on main: crates/drm-sys/Android.bp
//   404s in android-crates-io and in external/rust/crates,
//   and the r32 crates listing has no drm-sys entry - an
//   upstream gap (the drm-ffi 0.8.0 upgrade references a
//   crate never vendored), not a sync/prune issue. Stubbed
//   as rust_library with crate_name drm_sys (what drm-ffi
//   resolves with extern crate drm_sys), srcs lib.rs
//   (reused from the #96 libcxx stub), mirroring the libcxx
//   stub.
// COMPILE-STAGE CAVEATS (the next round may hit these if
// libdm / libfstab are actually compiled for this target -
// Soong only needed the stubs to parse): dm.cpp includes
// uuid/uuid.h and calls uuid_generate / uuid_unparse_lower;
// fstab.cpp includes libgsi/libgsi.h and uses gsi
// kDsuPostfix etc. A bare stub passes Soong; dummy headers
// plus stub functions will be needed only if the next run
// fails at compile/link.
cc_library {
    name: "libext2_uuid",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_headers {
    name: "libgsi_headers",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "libgsi",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "libgsid",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
rust_library {
    name: "libdrm_sys",
    crate_name: "drm_sys",
    srcs: ["lib.rs"],
    edition: "2021",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #116/#117/#118 fix: the #111/#112/#113 fix HELD in
// all three (prune step passed in 1-2s + pre-build guard
// passed). All three fail at Soong ninja generation,
// ~33-37s into the build step, on the SAME fix code (head
// 81f5407 - the #111/#112/#113 fix, workflow 8aeb025,
// rebased onto the save-always head 65709cd).
// Subset-reporting again: #116 reports 1 line, #117
// reports 2, #118 reports 3 - all different subsets of
// one commit. The fix covers the UNION (4 lines, 6
// instances). Raw-log verbatim (job-logs.txt, genuine
// build-output lines only - the 14 other "depends on
// undefined module" + 3 "missing variant" matches in each
// raw log are the runner echoing the Build step script
// itself, the comment block + the pre-build-guard echo
// commands that did NOT fire, NOT build errors):
//   #116 (45850213901, 14m10s, auto, manifest e0636fa) -
//   1 line: external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/gbm/
//   Android.bp:16:1 libgbm_rust depends on undefined
//   module libgbm_sys.
//   #117 (45850361596, 13m04s, auto, README 81f5407) -
//   2 lines: external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/
//   rusqlite/Android.bp:16:1 librusqlite depends on
//   undefined module liblibsqlite3_sys; + the libgbm_sys
//   line above.
//   #118 (45850678030, 15m10s, manual ~21:05 IST,
//   81f5407) - 3 lines: external/rust/android-crates-io/
//   crates/tokio-openssl/Android.bp:16:1 libtokio_openssl
//   depends on undefined module libbssl_sys; same file
//   depends on undefined module libopenssl; + the
//   libgbm_sys line above.
//   No genuine "missing variant" line in any of the three.
// Root causes, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 /
// AOSP android-15.0.0_r32:
// - libbssl_sys: rustlibs of the rust_library
//   libtokio_openssl (android-crates-io/crates/
//   tokio-openssl/Android.bp:16, r32; tokio-openssl 0.6.5,
//   rustlibs libbssl_sys + libopenssl + libtokio).
//   Upstream rust_library in external/boringssl/
//   Android.bp:913-914 (r32, crate_name bssl_sys,
//   host_supported, via rust_defaults libbssl_sys_defaults)
//   - external/boringssl is NOT synced (not in the
//   32-project manifest; only its cc stubs libssl /
//   libcrypto_static were stubbed in #105). Stubbed as
//   rust_library with crate_name bssl_sys.
// - libopenssl: rustlibs of the same libtokio_openssl.
//   Upstream rust_library in external/rust/crates/openssl
//   (r32, crate_name openssl) - external/rust/crates is
//   NOT synced. Stubbed as rust_library with crate_name
//   openssl.
// - libgbm_sys: rustlibs of the rust_library libgbm_rust
//   (android-crates-io/crates/gbm/Android.bp:16, r32). NO
//   defining file exists at r32 or on main: no crates/
//   gbm-sys repo under external/rust/crates and no
//   crates/gbm-sys dir in android-crates-io at r32 (its
//   tree has crates/gbm but no gbm-sys) - an upstream gap
//   (the gbm crate upgrade references a crate never
//   vendored), same pattern as libdrm_sys (#113). Stubbed
//   as rust_library with crate_name gbm_sys.
// - liblibsqlite3_sys: rustlibs of the rust_library
//   librusqlite (android-crates-io/crates/rusqlite/
//   Android.bp:16, r32). Upstream rust_library in
//   external/rust/crates/libsqlite3-sys (r32, crate_name
//   libsqlite3_sys, the rusqlite FFI crate) -
//   external/rust/crates is NOT synced. Stubbed as
//   rust_library with crate_name libsqlite3_sys.
// All four stubs use srcs lib.rs (reused from the #96
// libcxx stub), mirroring the libdrm_sys stub.
rust_library {
    name: "libbssl_sys",
    crate_name: "bssl_sys",
    srcs: ["lib.rs"],
    edition: "2021",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
rust_library {
    name: "libopenssl",
    crate_name: "openssl",
    srcs: ["lib.rs"],
    edition: "2021",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
rust_library {
    name: "libgbm_sys",
    crate_name: "gbm_sys",
    srcs: ["lib.rs"],
    edition: "2021",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
rust_library {
    name: "liblibsqlite3_sys",
    crate_name: "libsqlite3_sys",
    srcs: ["lib.rs"],
    edition: "2021",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #119/#120/#121 fix: the #116/#117/#118 fix HELD in
// all three (prune step passed + pre-build guard passed).
// All three fail at Soong ninja generation, ~35-53s into
// the build step, on the SAME fix code (head 5a83c08 - the
// #116/#117/#118 fix, workflow fa506ff). Subset-reporting
// again: #119 reports 10 lines, #120 reports 15, #121
// reports 7 - all different subsets of one commit. The fix
// covers the UNION (12 distinct modules, 15 error lines -
// #120's 15 lines are the full union; #119's 10 and #121's
// 7 are subsets of them). Raw-log verbatim (job logs,
// genuine build-output lines only - the other "error:"
// matches in each log are the runner echoing the Build
// step script itself, the pre-build-guard echo commands
// that did NOT fire, NOT build errors):
//   #119 (45857356942, 15m45s, auto, manifest 02209e6) -
//   10 lines: libsnapshot_cow (system/core/fs_mgr/
//   libsnapshot/Android.bp:201) needs
//   libupdate_engine_headers, libbrotli, liblz4,
//   libzstd, and libz missing variant; liblog-host-test
//   (system/logging/liblog/tests/Android.bp:139) needs
//   libgtest_isolated_main; libinput_from_rust_to_cpp
//   (frameworks/native/libs/input/Android.bp:176) needs
//   cxx-bridge-header; libexpresslog (system/core/
//   libstats/expresslog/Android.bp:29) needs
//   libtextclassifier_hash_headers +
//   libtextclassifier_hash_static; run_dex2oat_test
//   (frameworks/native/cmds/installd/Android.bp:126)
//   needs server_configurable_flags.
//   #120 (45857551439, 16m25s, auto, README 5a83c08) -
//   15 lines: the #119 set (same 10, different order) +
//   5 more: libaconfig_flags_rust (build/make/tools/
//   aconfig/aconfig_flags/Android.bp:36) +
//   libaconfig_test_rust_library (build/make/tools/
//   aconfig/aconfig/Android.bp:241) need libflags_rust;
//   libaconfig_storage_read_api_cc (aconfig/
//   aconfig_storage_read_api/Android.bp:80) +
//   libaconfig_storage_file_cc (aconfig/
//   aconfig_storage_file/Android.bp:121) need
//   cxx-bridge-header; libfs_avb (system/core/fs_mgr/
//   libfs_avb/Android.bp:27) needs libavb.
//   #121 (45857942449, 12m43s, manual ~21:51 IST,
//   5a83c08) - 7 lines: the libsnapshot_cow set (5) +
//   libgtest_isolated_main + cxx-bridge-header
//   (libinput_from_rust_to_cpp only).
//   CORRECTION: an early browser read of #121 reported
//   two vendor/qcom/opensource/power/config/Android.bp
//   "power.qcom / power.qcom.rc is not a module name"
//   lines - PHANTOM. A second exhaustive read of the
//   same job log (every error line + negative searches)
//   found no such lines in any of the three runs, and
//   the manifest syncs no vendor/qcom project, so that
//   file cannot exist in the synced tree. Same class as
//   the #30/#33/#84 phantom reads.
// Root causes, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 /
// AOSP android-15.0.0_r32 (all 12 defining projects
// UNSYNCED):
// - libupdate_engine_headers: header_libs of
//   libsnapshot_cow_defaults (system/core/fs_mgr/
//   libsnapshot/Android.bp:176-199, which the
//   cc_library_static libsnapshot_cow pulls in via
//   defaults). Upstream cc_library_headers in
//   system/update_engine/Android.bp (r32 lines
//   1313-1314) - system/update_engine NOT synced.
// - libbrotli: static_libs of the same defaults block.
//   Upstream cc_library_static in external/brotli/
//   Android.bp (r32 lines 49-50) - external/brotli NOT
//   synced.
// - liblz4: static_libs of the same defaults block.
//   Upstream plain cc_library in external/lz4/lib/
//   Android.bp (r32 lines 19-20; external/lz4/
//   Android.bp does not exist at r32) - external/lz4
//   NOT synced.
// - libzstd: static_libs of the same defaults block.
//   Upstream plain cc_library in external/zstd/
//   Android.bp (r32 lines 44-45) - external/zstd NOT
//   synced.
// - libz: static_libs of the same defaults block.
//   Upstream plain cc_library in external/zlib/
//   Android.bp (r32 lines 180-181) - external/zlib NOT
//   synced. The #96 stub was cc_library_shared, which
//   provides no static variant, so the static variant
//   the consumer requests is missing - same fix as
//   libjsoncpp (#105) and the protobuf stubs (#99):
//   change the stub to plain cc_library (it still
//   provides the shared variant liblibz_sys needs).
// - libgtest_isolated_main: NOT named in the consumer
//   file. liblog-host-test (cc_test_host, system/
//   logging/liblog/tests/Android.bp:139) sets isolated:
//   true, and Soong's cc/test.go appends
//   libgtest_isolated_main to the test's StaticLibs
//   automatically. Upstream cc_library_static in
//   system/testing/gtest_extras/gtest_isolated/
//   Android.bp (r32 lines 59-60, srcs Main.cpp,
//   host_supported; its whole_static_libs
//   libgtest_isolated + shared_libs liblog are NOT
//   replicated - bare stub, as usual) - system/testing/
//   gtest_extras NOT synced.
// - cxx-bridge-header: generated_headers of
//   libinput_from_rust_to_cpp (frameworks/native/libs/
//   input/Android.bp:189-190),
//   libaconfig_storage_read_api_cc (build/make/tools/
//   aconfig/aconfig_storage_read_api/Android.bp:80)
//   and libaconfig_storage_file_cc (aconfig/
//   aconfig_storage_file/Android.bp:121). Upstream
//   genrule in external/rust/cxx/Android.bp (r32 lines
//   93-98, tools cxxbridge, out rust/cxx.h) -
//   external/rust/cxx NOT synced, and NOT in
//   external/rust/crates/cxx (that path 404s). Stubbed
//   as a genrule with the same out and a cmd that
//   touches it - tools omitted (cxxbridge is unsynced)
//   and the rule never runs, since the consumers are
//   never built. If the next run errors on the genrule
//   stub, switch it to cc_library_headers.
// - libtextclassifier_hash_headers: header_libs of
//   libexpresslog (system/core/libstats/expresslog/
//   Android.bp:38-39). Upstream cc_library_headers in
//   external/libtextclassifier/native/Android.bp (r32
//   lines 24-25) - external/libtextclassifier NOT
//   synced.
// - libtextclassifier_hash_static: static_libs of the
//   same libexpresslog (lines 41-43). Upstream
//   cc_library_static in the same file (r32 lines
//   62-63) - the same-file sibling
//   libtextclassifier_hash (plain cc_library, lines
//   55-56) is NOT stubbed: no synced file references
//   it (unlike libgsi/libgsid in #111, which synced
//   fs_mgr code references) - stub it if a run
//   reports it.
// - server_configurable_flags: shared_libs of
//   run_dex2oat_test (frameworks/native/cmds/installd/
//   Android.bp:126; also installd_defaults). Upstream
//   plain cc_library in system/
//   server_configurable_flags/libflags/Android.bp (r32
//   lines 5-6) - system/server_configurable_flags NOT
//   synced.
// - libflags_rust: NOT named in either consumer file.
//   libaconfig_flags_rust (rust_aconfig_library,
//   build/make/tools/aconfig/aconfig_flags/
//   Android.bp:36-41) and libaconfig_test_rust_library
//   (rust_aconfig_library, aconfig/Android.bp:241-246)
//   have no rustlibs entry for it; Soong's
//   rust_aconfig_library SourceProviderDeps (build/
//   soong/aconfig/codegen/rust_aconfig_library.go)
//   appends libflags_rust to deps.Rustlibs for every
//   rust_aconfig_library. Upstream rust_library in
//   system/server_configurable_flags/libflags/
//   Android.bp (r32 lines 75-77, crate_name flags_rust,
//   srcs lib.rs, rustlibs libcxx) - same project as
//   above, NOT synced. The stub is bare (no rustlibs /
//   static_libs replicated), like the other rust stubs.
// - libavb: static_libs of libfs_avb
//   (cc_library_static, system/core/fs_mgr/libfs_avb/
//   Android.bp:43-44, alongside the synced libdm and
//   libfstab and the #111-stubbed libgsi). Upstream
//   cc_library_static in external/avb/Android.bp (r32
//   lines 195-196) - external/avb NOT synced.
// All stubs use srcs empty.c (cc) / lib.rs (rust),
// mirroring the existing stubs; the headers stubs have
// no srcs, like libgsi_headers /
// libstagefright_headers.
cc_library_headers {
    name: "libupdate_engine_headers",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libbrotli",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "liblz4",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "libzstd",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libgtest_isolated_main",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
genrule {
    name: "cxx-bridge-header",
    out: ["rust/cxx.h"],
    cmd: "touch $(out)",
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_headers {
    name: "libtextclassifier_hash_headers",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libtextclassifier_hash_static",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "server_configurable_flags",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
rust_library {
    name: "libflags_rust",
    crate_name: "flags_rust",
    srcs: ["lib.rs"],
    edition: "2021",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libavb",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #122/#123/#124 fix: the #119/#120/#121 fix HELD in
// all three (prune step passed + pre-build guard passed).
// All three fail at Soong ninja generation, ~36-54s into
// the build step, on the SAME fix code (head a5b3730 - the
// #119/#120/#121 fix, workflow d0b8b17). Subset-reporting
// again: #122 reports 11 lines, #123 reports 10, #124
// reports 15 - all different subsets of one commit. The fix
// covers the UNION (17 distinct lines, 10 distinct modules;
// #122's 11 lines are all inside the #124+#123 union).
// Raw-log verbatim (job-logs.txt, genuine build-output
// lines only - the other "error:" matches in each log are
// the runner echoing the Build step script itself, the
// pre-build-guard echo commands that did NOT fire, NOT
// build errors). The FAILED line is
// out/soong/build.yuzora_lights.ninja (not build.ninja),
// and Soong prints no "N errors" total line this round.
//   #122 (45867347789, 15m0s, auto, manifest b35b3cd) -
//   11 lines: liblp needs libext4_utils; inspect_cow +
//   create_snapshot need libgflags; libfs_avb_test_util
//   needs libavb_host_sysdeps + libchrome; write_cow
//   needs libgflags; create_snapshot needs libext4_utils;
//   libhidl-gen needs libhwbinder_headers; libvbmeta_test
//   + create_snapshot + libhidl-gen need libcrypto static
//   variant.
//   #123 (45867671751, 15m22s, auto, README a5b3730) -
//   10 lines: the #122 set minus libvbmeta_test/libcrypto
//   and the libfs_avb pair, plus libsnapuserd needs
//   libext4_utils + liburing.
//   #124 (45867963752, 15m59s, manual ~22:58 IST,
//   a5b3730) - 15 lines: the #122 set (same 11) + 4 more:
//   libtracing_perfetto needs libperfetto_c +
//   android.os.flags-aconfig-cc-host; libapex needs
//   libziparchive + libselinux shared variant.
//   NOTE on paths: the raw logs cite the consumers as
//   system/core/liblp/Android.bp:31:1 and
//   system/apex/apexd/Android.bp:271:1, but at
//   lineage-22.2 liblp lives at system/core/fs_mgr/liblp/
//   and libapex starts at apexd/Android.bp:527
//   (libapex-deps at 492) - Soong attributes through the
//   defaults: expansion, so the :line numbers do not
//   reproduce in the raw files. Key the fix off module
//   names, not :line numbers (same caveat as the #96
//   "librusb_platform" and #107 aconfig-path misreads).
// Root causes, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 /
// AOSP android-15.0.0_r32 (all defining projects UNSYNCED):
// - libext4_utils: shared_libs (liblp, via the
//   liblp_lib_deps variable), static_libs (create_snapshot,
//   libsnapuserd, liblp_test_defaults) and whole_static_libs
//   (libsnaphot_defaults) - only plain cc_library satisfies
//   all three. Upstream plain cc_library in
//   system/extras/ext4_utils/Android.bp (r32 ~lines 41-45,
//   host_supported) - system/extras NOT synced.
// - libgflags: static_libs of inspect_cow, create_snapshot
//   (host-only binary) and write_cow. Upstream plain
//   cc_library in external/gflags/Android.bp (r32 ~line
//   107, host_supported via gflags_defaults) - external/
//   gflags NOT synced. (Not cc_library_static: the 2017
//   port was static; at r32 it is plain cc_library.)
// - libavb_host_sysdeps: static_libs of libfs_avb_test_util
//   (via libfs_avb_host_test_defaults). Upstream
//   cc_library_host_static in external/avb/Android.bp
//   (r32 ~line 627, host-only by type, no host_supported
//   property upstream - the stub mirrors that) -
//   external/avb NOT synced. Different module from libavb
//   (cc_library_static, same file, stubbed in #119).
// - libchrome: shared_libs of libfs_avb_test_util (via
//   libfs_avb_host_test_defaults). Upstream plain
//   cc_library in external/libchrome/Android.bp (r32
//   ~line 1657, host_supported, min_sdk_version 30;
//   its visibility list names //system/core/fs_mgr/libfs_avb)
//   - external/libchrome NOT synced. NOT
//   libchrome-gestures_headers (already stubbed, different
//   module). Caveat: upstream libchrome is the full
//   Chromium base; a bare stub passes Soong only - if a
//   later run fails at compile/link on libchrome symbols,
//   that is a new layer (same caveat as libdm/libfstab #111).
// - libhwbinder_headers: header_libs of libhidl-gen.
//   Upstream cc_library_headers in system/libhwbinder/
//   Android.bp (r32 ~line 67, host_supported,
//   export_include_dirs include) - system/libhwbinder
//   NOT synced.
// - libperfetto_c: shared_libs of libtracing_perfetto
//   (cc_library_shared, host_supported). Upstream
//   cc_library_shared in external/perfetto/Android.bp
//   (r32; on main it is plain cc_library - r32 is
//   authoritative, do not copy the main-branch type) -
//   external/perfetto NOT synced.
// - android.os.flags-aconfig-cc-host: shared_libs of
//   libtracing_perfetto. Upstream cc_aconfig_library in
//   frameworks/base/AconfigFlags.bp (lineage-22.2 lines
//   918-926, aconfig_declarations android.os.flags-aconfig,
//   host_supported) - frameworks/base NOT synced. It is
//   explicitly declared (unlike libflags_rust #119, which
//   Soong appends implicitly); a cc_aconfig_library
//   generates a cc_library of the same name, so a plain
//   cc_library stub satisfies it. Siblings -cc / -cc-test
//   are NOT stubbed - no synced file references them;
//   stub them if a run reports one.
// - libziparchive: shared_libs of libapex (via
//   libapex-deps). Upstream plain cc_library in
//   system/libziparchive/Android.bp (lineage-22.2 lines
//   284-300, host_supported via libziparchive_lib_defaults)
//   - system/libziparchive NOT synced (its own project,
//   not under system/core).
// - liburing: static_libs of libsnapuserd (also
//   snapuserd_defaults/_test_defaults/_extractor).
//   Upstream cc_library_static in external/liburing/
//   Android.bp (r32, host_supported) - external/liburing
//   NOT synced.
// - libcrypto: the #96 cc_library_shared stub provides no
//   static variant; the host consumers (libvbmeta_test,
//   create_snapshot, libhidl-gen, all static_libs on
//   linux_glibc) need it. Upstream plain cc_library in
//   external/boringssl/Android.bp (r32 ~line 497,
//   host_supported via libcrypto_defaults) - the device
//   static variant is disabled upstream (FIPS; static
//   users take libcrypto_static, already stubbed), but
//   the HOST static variant is built, so plain cc_library
//   is the fix - same as libjsoncpp (#105), libz (#119)
//   and the protobuf stubs (#99). The stub changes
//   from cc_library_shared to plain cc_library above.
// - libselinux: the #78 cc_library_static stub provides no
//   shared variant; libapex needs the shared host variant
//   (shared_libs via libapex-deps). Upstream plain
//   cc_library in external/selinux/libselinux/Android.bp
//   (r32, host_supported) - external/selinux NOT synced.
//   The stub changes from cc_library_static to plain
//   cc_library above (same fix as libcrypto).
