// all three (prune step passed + pre-build guard passed).
// All three fail at Soong ninja generation, tens of seconds
// into the build step, on the SAME fix code (head 24b86f6 -
// the #138/#139/#140 fix, workflow eed9b31; #141 is the
// manifest push 026e1af, #142 the README push 24b86f6 -
// same workflow file in all three, #143 a manual dispatch
// ~05:08 IST on 24b86f6). NO subset variation this round:
// all three report the IDENTICAL 12 lines - the fix covers
// that set (12 lines, 9 distinct modules). Runs #141
// (45911630805, 13m27s, auto, manifest 026e1af) + #142
// (45911747029, 15m56s, auto, README 24b86f6) + #143
// (45912149579, 13m43s, manual ~05:08 IST, 24b86f6).
// CORRECTION to the run #141 id: the first browser read
// was given 45911955969, which 404s - the runs list shows
// #141 is 45911630805. Always take run ids from the runs
// list, never from a dispatch handoff alone.
// Raw-log verbatim (live browser read of the job-logs.txt
// raw logs; genuine build-output lines only - the other
// "error:" matches in each log are the runner echoing the
// Build step script itself, the pre-build-guard echo
// commands that did NOT fire, NOT build errors). The
// FAILED line is out/soong/build.yuzora_lights.ninja (not
// build.ninja). No genuine "missing variant" line in any
// of the three runs.
//   libinputflinger_base (frameworks/native/services/
//   inputflinger/Android.bp:229) needs libstatslog.
//   libinput_tests (frameworks/native/libs/input/tests/
//   Android.bp:11) needs libflagtest + libstatslog.
//   inputflinger_tests (frameworks/native/services/
//   inputflinger/tests/Android.bp:34) needs
//   libpalmrejection + libperfetto_client_experimental +
//   perfetto_winscope_extensions_zero + libchrome-gestures
//   + libflagtest + android.hardware.input.processor-
//   V1-ndk + libkll + libstatspull + libstatslog.
// NOTE on :line numbers: Soong's :229 / :11 / :34 ARE the
// module block starts in the live files this round
// (verified against the manifest-pinned tree:
// libinputflinger_base cc_library_shared block at :229,
// libinput_tests cc_test block at :11, inputflinger_tests
// cc_test block at :34) - the deps themselves arrive through
// the defaults the three targets inherit
// (libinputflinger_base_defaults,
// libinputflinger_defaults, libinputdispatcher_defaults,
// libinputreader_defaults), so key the fix off module
// names, not :line numbers (same caveat as the #122
// liblp/libapex paths and the #125 fastboot/init lines).
// CORRECTION to the browser reports: both browser reads
// claimed the prune step "removed frameworks/native/
// services/inputflinger, frameworks/native/libs/input and
// frameworks/native/libs/sensor" - WRONG. The prune step
// contains no rm for any of those trees (verified in this
// file); the three consumers are test targets in the
// SYNCED frameworks/native tree, and their missing deps
// are stubbed, not pruned. Same phantom class as the
// #30/#33/#84/#96/#107/#121/#131 misreads - the raw log
// error lines are authoritative, the browser's prune
// summary is not.
// Root causes, verified live at LineageOS lineage-22.2 /
// AOSP android-15.0.0_r32 (all defining projects UNSYNCED
// unless noted):
// - libstatslog: the StatsD client log lib. In Android 12
//   the StatsD module code moved from system/core/libstats
//   to packages/modules/StatsD (source.android.com statsd
//   doc: system/core/libstats -> packages/modules/StatsD/
//   lib/libstats) - packages/modules/StatsD is NOT synced;
//   the defining .bp file was NOT traced to a file this
//   round (same class as the #105 libgtest_isolated /
//   libprocinfo stubs - home not traced). Used in
//   shared_libs by libinputflinger_base_defaults,
//   libinputflinger_defaults, libinputdispatcher_defaults
//   and libinputreader_defaults, and directly by
//   libinput_tests, so a plain cc_library stub satisfies
//   it.
// - libstatspull: the StatsD pull-atom client lib -
//   cc_library in packages/modules/StatsD/lib/
//   libstatspull (same Android 12 move: system/core/
//   libstats/pull -> packages/modules/StatsD/lib/
//   libstatspull; the prebuilt module SDK confirms the
//   shared lib) - packages/modules/StatsD is NOT synced.
//   Used in shared_libs by libinputflinger_defaults,
//   libinputdispatcher_defaults and libinputreader_
//   defaults, so a plain cc_library stub satisfies it.
// - libkll: provides kll.h, included by the inputflinger
//   dispatcher (LatencyAggregator.h) - the defining .bp
//   file was NOT traced to a file this round (same class
//   as the #105 stubs - home not traced). Used in
//   shared_libs by libinputflinger_defaults and
//   libinputdispatcher_defaults, so a plain cc_library
//   stub satisfies it.
// - libflagtest: the aconfig flag-test helper lib - also
//   used in static_libs by cts/flags/cc_tests
//   FlagMacrosTest; the defining .bp file was NOT traced
//   to a file this round (same class as the #105 stubs -
//   home not traced). Used in static_libs by
//   libinput_tests + inputflinger_tests, so a plain
//   cc_library stub satisfies it (plain builds the static
//   variant).
// - libpalmrejection: the Chromium neural palm-detection
//   model lib used by the input code (frameworks/native
//   commits, bug 198472780 - "The libpalmrejection
//   library is going to be used in the input code"); the
//   defining .bp file was NOT traced to a file this round
//   (same class as the #105 stubs - home not traced).
//   Used in static_libs by libinputflinger_defaults, so a
//   plain cc_library stub satisfies it.
// - libperfetto_client_experimental: the Perfetto client
//   API lib - GN target //:libperfetto_client_
//   experimental, translated to Android.bp cc_library by
//   external/perfetto/tools/gen_android_bp (a default
//   target; host_supported, vendor_available) -
//   external/perfetto is NOT synced. Used in static_libs
//   by libinputflinger_defaults and libinputdispatcher_
//   defaults, so a plain cc_library stub satisfies it.
// - perfetto_winscope_extensions_zero: a Perfetto proto
//   lib (the *_zero proto variant) in external/perfetto;
//   the defining .bp file was NOT traced to a file this
//   round (same class as the #105 stubs - home not
//   traced). Used in static_libs by libinputdispatcher_
//   defaults, so a plain cc_library stub satisfies it.
// - libchrome-gestures: cc_library in external/
//   libchrome-gestures (an AOSP submodule - .gitmodules;
//   the sibling libchrome-gestures_headers was already
//   stubbed in #84) - external/libchrome-gestures is NOT
//   synced. Used in static_libs by libinputreader_
//   defaults (+ libinputreader) and in whole_static_libs
//   by libinputreader_static, so only a plain cc_library
//   stub satisfies both (plain builds the static
//   variant).
// - android.hardware.input.processor-V1-ndk: the generated
//   NDK lib of the aidl_interface android.hardware.input.
//   processor in hardware/interfaces/input/processor/aidl/
//   Android.bp (verified in the synced tree: frozen
//   version 1, cpp/java backends disabled, ndk default-
//   on, stability vintf, imports android.hardware.input.
//   common-V1) - hardware/interfaces is synced but the
//   closure prune keeps ONLY light/aidl +
//   compatibility_matrices + common/aidl + input/common/
//   aidl, so input/processor is pruned. The imported
//   android.hardware.input.common-V1 needs NO stub: its
//   aidl dir is kept (the #65/#66/#67 fix). Used in
//   shared_libs by libinputflinger_defaults, so a plain
//   cc_library stub satisfies it.
// COMPILE-STAGE CAVEAT: all 9 stubs are bare plain
// cc_library stubs (srcs empty.c, no headers), as all
// earlier plain stubs were. A bare stub passes Soong;
// dummy headers + stub symbols will be needed only if a
// later run gets past Soong and fails at compile/link
// because the test sources actually include these libs'
// headers (LatencyAggregator.h includes <kll.h>; the
// inputflinger/input test sources include palm, perfetto
// and gestures headers) - same class as the #111 libgsi
// and #135 flatbuffer caveats. Note the lights HAL
// closure itself does not link these test targets, so
// this caveat may never materialize.
cc_library {
    name: "libstatslog",
