// Runs #147/#148/#149 fix: the #144/#145/#146 fix HELD in
// all three (prune step passed in 4s + pre-build guard
// passed; ZERO Soong dependency-cycle lines in any raw
// log - the libwinpthread stl: "none" fix resolved).
// All three fail at Soong ninja-file generation, 36-46s
// into the build step, on the SAME fix code (head
// d227a64 - the #144/#145/#146 fix, workflow 996034f;
// #147 is the manifest push 9e61ecc, #148 the README
// push d227a64 - same workflow file in all three, #149
// a manual dispatch ~06:22 IST on d227a64). Subset
// variation again: #149 reports 3 lines, #147/#148
// report 4 - the fix covers the UNION (4 lines, 3
// distinct modules). Runs #147 (45918788481, 15m37s,
// auto) + #148 (45918894728, 13m21s, auto) + #149
// (45919249035, 14m43s, manual ~06:22 IST).
// Raw-log verbatim error union (live browser read of
// the job-logs.txt raw logs; genuine build-output
// lines only - the other "error:" matches in each
// log are the runner echoing the Build step script
// itself, the pre-build-guard echo commands that did
// NOT fire, NOT build errors; no genuine "missing
// variant" line in any run):
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:2180:1:
//     "librust_baremetal" depends on undefined module
//     "//external/llvm-libc:llvmlibc".
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:2180:1:
//     "librust_baremetal" depends on undefined module
//     "libarm-optimized-routines-mem".
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:234:1:
//     "libc_jemalloc_wrapper" depends on undefined
//     module "libjemalloc5".
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:841:1: "libc_bionic"
//     depends on undefined module
//     "//external/llvm-libc:llvmlibc". (#147/#148 only)
//   FAILED: out/soong/build.yuzora_lights.ninja.
// CORRECTION: the first UI-log read of #149 reported
// the module as "//external/llvm-libc:llvm-libc" -
// WRONG; the raw log says "//external/llvm-libc:
// llvmlibc", matching the consumer's reference
// (bionic/libc/Android.bp:2209). Same phantom class
// as the #96 "librusb_platform" misread - raw-log
// lines are authoritative. Line numbers verified
// against the manifest-pinned tree: the
// librust_baremetal block starts at :2181 (Soong
// :2180:1), libc_jemalloc_wrapper at :235 (Soong
// :234:1), and libc_bionic's whole_static_libs at
// :1258 (Soong :841:1 - attributes through the
// defaults expansion again, same caveat as the #122
// liblp/libapex paths and the #125 fastboot/init
// lines). Key the fix off module names, not :line
// numbers.
// Root causes, verified live at AOSP
// android-15.0.0_r32 (which IS the LineageOS
// lineage-22.2 source for these three paths - the
// LineageOS manifest pins the AOSP remote to r32
// and no LineageOS mirrors exist for these repos;
// all three defining projects UNSYNCED):
// - llvmlibc is cc_library_static in
//   external/llvm-libc/Android.bp (r32, lines 24-25),
//   stl: "none", visibility //bionic/libc. Used in
//   whole_static_libs by librust_baremetal (:2209)
//   and libc_bionic (:1258).
// - libarm-optimized-routines-mem/-string/-math are
//   all cc_library_static in external/arm-optimized-
//   routines/Android.bp (r32, lines 187-188, 137-138,
//   84-85); -mem carries stl: "none", nocrt,
//   visibility //bionic/libc (comment: "Memory
//   intrinsics for bare-metal Rust binaries."); the
//   shared defaults carry stl: "none" +
//   host_supported. -mem used in whole_static_libs
//   by librust_baremetal (:2210).
// - libjemalloc5 is plain cc_library in
//   external/jemalloc_new/Android.bp (r32, lines
//   185-186) - NOT external/jemalloc (no Android.bp
//   there at r32); target.android.shared disabled,
//   defaults carry stl: "none" + host_supported.
//   Used in static_libs by libc_jemalloc_wrapper
//   (:242) and in whole_static_libs via the
//   cc_defaults libc_native_allocator_defaults
//   (:206/:220, product_variables malloc_low_memory
//   - gated, which is why no "libc" module error
//   surfaces). Sibling libjemalloc5_je_prefixed is
//   cc_library_host_static (same file, lines
//   235-236) - a different module, already stubbed
//   in #96.
// - Siblings (same-file, next subset-reporting
//   layer, #111 libgsi/libgsid precedent):
//   libarm-optimized-routines-string in
//   whole_static_libs by libc_common (bionic/libc/
//   Android.bp:1369) and libarm-optimized-routines-
//   math in whole_static_libs by libm (bionic/libm/
//   Android.bp:33). Neither errored in any run, but
//   both are one subset-reporting layer away, so
//   both are stubbed now.
// Why llvmlibc cannot live in yuzora-stubs: the dep
// is path-qualified (//external/llvm-libc:llvmlibc),
// so Soong resolves it only in package
// external/llvm-libc. The prune step creates
// external/llvm-libc/Android.bp (+ empty.c) each
// run - same mechanism as the #131 .aidl creation.
// No new projects in the manifest (still 32); the
// dir is created by the workflow, not synced. All 5
// stubs carry stl: "none" (upstream carries it on
// all five via the module or its defaults; the
// empty.c stub needs no STL; it also avoids a
// libwinpthread-class default-STL dep).
// COMPILE-STAGE CAVEAT: all 5 stubs are bare (srcs
// empty.c, no real symbols). libc_common /
// libc_bionic / libc_jemalloc_wrapper are in the
// libc closure, so if the next run passes Soong and
// links libc.so, undefined symbols from the empty
// stubs may surface (memcpy/memset/memmove et al.
// from the -string/-mem stubs, strlcpy/strlcat/
// memrchr/bsearch from llvmlibc, malloc/calloc/
// realloc/free from libjemalloc5 if jemalloc is
// selected) - dummy implementations will be needed
// only then, same class as the #111 libgsi / #135
// flatbuffer caveats. librust_baremetal is NOT in
// the HAL closure (baremetal Rust for AVF guests),
// so its two deps may never link.
cc_library_static {
    name: "libarm-optimized-routines-mem",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    system_shared_libs: [],
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libarm-optimized-routines-string",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    system_shared_libs: [],
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libarm-optimized-routines-math",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    system_shared_libs: [],
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "libjemalloc5",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    system_shared_libs: [],
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #150/#151/#152 fix: the #147/#148/#149 fix HELD in
// all three (prune step passed in 1s + pre-build guard
// passed; ZERO llvmlibc / libjemalloc5 /
// libarm-optimized-routines lines in any raw log). All
// three fail at Soong ninja-file generation, 35-37s into
// the build step, on the SAME fix code (head 5a43a82 -
// the #147/#148/#149 fix, workflow 05ebd43; #150 is the
// manifest push 261cf27, #151 the README push 5a43a82 -
// same workflow file in all three, #152 a manual
// dispatch ~07:15 IST on 5a43a82). NO subset variation
// this round: all three report the identical 2 lines.
// Runs #150 (45923995039, 12m51s, auto) + #151
// (45924127939, 13m45s, auto) + #152 (45924377917,
// 13m21s, manual ~07:15 IST).
// Raw-log verbatim error union (live browser read of
// the job-logs.txt raw logs; genuine build-output
// lines only - the other "error:" matches in each
// log are the runner echoing the Build step script
// itself, the pre-build-guard echo commands that did
// NOT fire, NOT build errors; no genuine "missing
// variant" line in any run):
//   error: system/core/fastboot/Android.bp:374:1:
//     "fastboot_test" depends on undefined module
//     "AdbWinApi".
//   error: system/core/fastboot/Android.bp:335:1:
//     "fastboot" depends on undefined module
//     "AdbWinApi".
//   FAILED: out/soong/build.yuzora_lights.ninja.
// PHANTOM CORRECTION: the first UI-log read of #152
// invented 'hardware/samsung/lights/Android.bp:26:1:
// module "android.hardware.lights-service.samsung"
// ... missing dependencies: AdbWinApi' - WRONG. The
// raw log has NO such line; no lights/ dir exists in
// the fork (live lineage-22.2 tree verified: no
// lights/, the HAL is aidl/light/Android.bp defining
// the singular android.hardware.light-service.samsung);
// the only genuine Soong errors are the two fastboot
// lines above. Same phantom class as #30/#33/#84/#96/
// #107/#131 - raw-log lines are authoritative. Line
// numbers verified against the manifest-pinned tree:
// the fastboot block starts at :336 (Soong :335:1)
// and fastboot_test at :375 (Soong :374:1) - Soong
// attributes through the defaults expansion by one
// line, same caveat as the #122 liblp/libapex paths
// and the #125 fastboot/init lines. Key the fix off
// module names, not :line numbers.
// Usage (synced system/core/fastboot/Android.bp):
// fastboot (cc_binary_host) target.windows.required
// ["AdbWinUsbApi"] + target.windows.shared_libs
// ["AdbWinApi"]; fastboot_test (cc_test_host)
// target.windows.shared_libs ["AdbWinApi"] + a
// windows_x86_64 enabled:false block ("Avoid trying
// to build for win64"). The dep is windows-x86-only
// (32-bit), matching upstream compile_multilib "32".
// Root causes, verified live at AOSP
// android-15.0.0_r32 (which IS the LineageOS
// lineage-22.2 source for these paths - the
// LineageOS manifest pins the AOSP remote to r32;
// the defining project development is UNSYNCED):
// AdbWinApi + AdbWinUsbApi are BOTH
// cc_prebuilt_library_shared in development/host/
// windows/Android.bp (r32, 32 lines; AdbWinApi
// lines 19-26, AdbWinUsbApi lines 28-32), sharing
// the cc_defaults AdbWinApi_defaults (lines 5-17:
// host_supported true, enabled false,
// device_supported false, compile_multilib "32",
// target.windows.enabled true). AdbWinApi: srcs
// prebuilt/usb/AdbWinApi.dll, windows_import_lib
// prebuilt/usb/AdbWinApi.lib, export_include_dirs
// ["usb/api"]. AdbWinUsbApi: srcs prebuilt/usb/
// AdbWinUsbApi.dll. Both are prebuilt DLLs - no DLL
// is available here, so the stubs are plain
// cc_library with srcs empty.c (plain builds both
// static and shared variants, satisfying the
// shared_libs use - same reasoning as libssl #105 /
// libcrypto #122 / libz #119). CORRECTIONS to the
// first guesses: system/libadbwinapi/Android.bp
// does NOT exist at r32 (no such repo; the phantom
// UI read's citation was invented), and
// development/host/windows/usb/api/Android.bp does
// NOT exist at r32 either (that dir holds legacy
// VS/MAKEFILE sources, no .bp). Both stubs carry
// stl: "none" (upstream carries none - the real
// modules are prebuilts; the empty.c stub needs no
// STL, and it avoids a libwinpthread-class
// default-STL dep). Both carry host_supported: true
// + target windows enabled (the #78 shape - the dep
// is windows-only).
// AdbWinUsbApi is stubbed too although no run
// errored on it: it sits in the same target.windows
// block of the same consumer (fastboot :364,
// required) - one subset-reporting layer away
// (#111 sibling precedent); required-only deps never
// errored in any run, but the stub costs one block
// and a re-run costs 13 min.
// COMPILE-STAGE CAVEAT: both stubs are bare (srcs
// empty.c, no real symbols, no DLL). fastboot /
// fastboot_test are host tools NOT in the HAL
// closure - the lights target never links them - so
// the empty stubs can never surface at link time
// here; they exist only so Soong's dependency
// resolution passes. Same class as the #111 libgsi
// caveat, but weaker: not even a theoretical link.
cc_library {
    name: "AdbWinApi",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library {
    name: "AdbWinUsbApi",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    host_supported: true,
    target: { windows: { enabled: true } },
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #153/#154/#155 fix: runs #153 (45929013520,
// 15m37s, auto, manifest 71371a6), #154 (45929119919,
// 13m20s, auto, README 1732445) and #155 (45929338979,
// 12m50s, manual dispatch ~08:06 IST 2026-11-27, head
// 1732445 - the runs #150/#151/#152 fix, workflow
// ebb5a3d) ALL FAILED at Soong ninja-file generation,
// 35-46s into the build step, on the SAME fix code.
// The #150/#151/#152 fix HELD in all three (prune step
// passed in 0-4s + pre-build guard passed; ZERO
// undefined-module / missing-variant lines in any raw
// log). NO subset variation this round: all three
// report the identical 7-line cycle. Raw-log verbatim
// (browser job-logs.txt read of all three raw logs;
// the other "error:" matches are the runner echoing
// the Build step script itself - the pre-build-guard
// echo commands that did not fire - NOT build errors):
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:1653:1: encountered
//     dependency cycle:
//   error: yuzora-stubs/Android.bp:1515:1: module
//     "gwp_asan_headers" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a" depends on module
//     "libc" variant "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared"
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:1653:1: module
//     "libc" variant "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared"
//     depends on module "libc" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared_current"
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:1653:1: module
//     "libc" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared_current" depends
//     on module "libc" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared_30"
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:1653:1: module
//     "libc" variant "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared_30"
//     depends on module "libc" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared_29"
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:1653:1: module
//     "libc" variant "android_arm64_armv8-a_shared_29"
//     depends on module "libc" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a_static"
//   error: bionic/libc/Android.bp:1653:1: module
//     "libc" variant "android_arm64_armv8-a_static"
//     depends on module "gwp_asan_headers" variant
//     "android_arm64_armv8-a"
//   FAILED: out/soong/build.yuzora_lights.ninja.
// Root cause, verified in the SYNCED Soong source
// (build/soong/cc): (1) every cc module gets an
// implicit dep on libc + libm + libdl -
// baseLinker.linkerDeps (linker.go) gives every cc
// module a default system_shared_libs (the toolchain's
// DefaultSharedLibraries; config/bionic.go: libc,
// libm, libdl) unless the module declines it, and
// appends them to LateSharedLibs. The bare
// gwp_asan_headers stub (cc_library_headers, #96 fix)
// carries no system_shared_libs, so it depends on
// libc shared. (2) The real libc depends back on the
// stub: libc_native_allocator_defaults
// (bionic/libc/Android.bp:199, manifest-pinned tree)
// has header_libs: ["gwp_asan_headers"], and libc
// uses that defaults via libc_library_defaults. The
// two edges close a cycle. The fix is
// system_shared_libs: [] on the stub - the sanctioned
// decline (linker.go: "If an empty list [] is
// specified, it implies that the module declines the
// default system_shared_libs"), the same property
// bionic's own modules carry (libc_defaults, and the
// cc_library_headers bionic_libc_platform_headers in
// the same file). Same class as the #144 libwinpthread
// cycle (an implicit dep on a stub), but the implicit
// dep here is system_shared_libs, not the default STL.
// CORRECTION to the #144-body claim: the cycle check
// does NOT run "once all modules resolve". Blueprint
// runs the cycle check (updateDependencies) at the end
// of each mutator group (build/blueprint/context.go
// runMutator) and a cycle found there replaces the
// errors that group collected - which is why
// #153/#154/#155 report ONLY the cycle even though
// libc's defaults also reference the undefined
// gwp_asan + libscudo below: those surface only once
// the cycle is fixed.
// THE WHOLE CLASS, fixed now (Soong reports one cycle
// per run - the #144 precedent - so fixing only the
// reported edge would cost one 13-minute round per
// cycle): system_shared_libs: [] is added to every cc
// stub the real libc / libm / libdl closure consumes:
// gwp_asan_headers (header_libs by
// libc_native_allocator_defaults);
// libarm-optimized-routines-string (whole_static_libs
// by libc_common, itself whole_static_libs by
// libc_common_static, itself whole_static_libs by
// libc); libarm-optimized-routines-math
// (whole_static_libs by libm, which carries
// target.bionic.system_shared_libs ["libc"]);
// libarm-optimized-routines-mem (whole_static_libs by
// librust_baremetal - no path back from libc, but the
// property is inert on an empty stub and kills the
// class); libjemalloc5 (static_libs by
// libc_jemalloc_wrapper - only via the
// malloc_low_memory-gated product_variable, same inert
// reasoning); llvmlibc (whole_static_libs by
// libc_bionic, itself whole_static_libs by
// libc_common). All five keep their types and
// stl: "none".
// NEW STUBS (same round): gwp_asan + libscudo are
// referenced unconditionally by libc's own defaults -
// gwp_asan in whole_static_libs by
// libc_library_defaults (static: + shared:,
// bionic/libc/Android.bp:1567/:1576) and libscudo in
// whole_static_libs by libc_native_allocator_defaults
// (:193) - and NEITHER is defined anywhere in the
// synced tree (no *.bp defines them) nor stubbed
// before now: they are the undefined-module layer the
// cycle was masking, stubbed now (#111 sibling
// precedent) so the next run does not spend 13 minutes
// reporting them. Both are static allocator libraries
// whole-archived into libc (external/gwp-asan +
// external/scudo, both UNSYNCED), so both stubs are
// cc_library_static with srcs empty.c, stl: "none"
// (the #147 whole_static_libs-only shape) - and both
// carry system_shared_libs: [] from birth, since libc
// consumes them directly and they would cycle on their
// first run without it. Upstream .bp types were NOT
// re-verified line-by-line at r32 this round (web
// search did not surface the files); the type follows
// the use (whole_static_libs only) - if a later run
// needs a shared variant, change to plain cc_library
// (the libcrypto / libselinux / libz / libjsoncpp
// precedent). NOT stubbed: tzdata_prebuilt +
// tz_version_prebuilt (required: by
// libc_library_defaults - required: never errored in
// 150 runs) and libc_musl_headers (musl-target-gated,
// the using modules are enabled: false outside musl).
// COMPILE-STAGE CAVEAT: the two new stubs are bare
// (empty.c, no symbols) and both sit in the libc
// closure (libc whole-archives them), so if the next
// run passes Soong and links libc.so, undefined
// gwp_asan_ / scudo symbols may surface - dummy
// implementations only then, same class as the #147
// llvmlibc / -string / -mem / libjemalloc5 caveat.
cc_library_static {
    name: "gwp_asan",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    system_shared_libs: [],
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libscudo",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "none",
    system_shared_libs: [],
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #156/#157/#158 fix: runs #156 (45935286393, 16m34s,
// auto, manifest a9d18f4), #157 (45935437929, 12m48s, auto,
// README 82c941c) and #158 (45935609318, 12m47s, manual
// dispatch ~09:11 IST 2026-11-27, head 82c941c - the runs
// #153/#154/#155 fix, workflow 61ded3f) ALL FAILED at Soong
// ninja-file generation, ~37s into the build step, on the
// SAME fix code. The #153/#154/#155 fix HELD in all three
// (prune step passed in 2-4s + pre-build guard passed;
// ZERO dependency-cycle lines in any raw log - the
// gwp_asan/libscudo system_shared_libs fix resolved).
// Subset variation again: #156 reports 8 lines, #157/#158
// report 7. The fix covers the UNION (8 lines, 6 distinct
// modules). Raw-log verbatim error union (browser
// job-logs.txt read of all three raw logs; the other
// "error:" matches in each log are the runner echoing the
// Build step script itself - the pre-build-guard echo
// commands that did not fire - NOT build errors; no
// genuine "missing variant" line in any run):
//   error: system/core/libgrallocusage/Android.bp:32:1:
//     "libgrallocusage" depends on undefined module
//     "android.hardware.graphics.allocator@2.0".
//   error: system/core/libstats/pull_lazy/Android.bp:8:1:
//     "libstatspull_lazy" depends on undefined module
//     "libstatspull_headers".
//   error: system/core/libstats/pull_lazy/Android.bp:8:1:
//     "libstatspull_lazy" depends on undefined module
//     "libstatssocket_headers".
//   error: frameworks/native/vulkan/vkjson/Android.bp:43:1:
//     "libvkjson_ndk" depends on undefined module
//     "vulkan_headers".
//   error: frameworks/native/vulkan/vkjson/Android.bp:43:1:
//     "libvkjson_ndk" depends on undefined module
//     "libjsoncpp_ndk".
//   error: frameworks/native/vulkan/vkprofiles/Android.bp:44:1:
//     "libvkprofiles_ndk" depends on undefined module
//     "vulkan_headers".
//   error: system/core/libstats/socket_lazy/Android.bp:8:1:
//     "libstatssocket_lazy" depends on undefined module
//     "libstatssocket_headers".
//   error: prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/Android.bp:48:1:
//     "libomp" depends on undefined module "ndk_system".
//     (#156 only)
// Root causes, verified live at AOSP android-15.0.0_r32 /
// LineageOS lineage-22.2 (all 6 defining projects
// UNSYNCED unless noted):
// android.hardware.graphics.allocator@2.0 is hidl_interface
// in hardware/interfaces/graphics/allocator/2.0/Android.bp
// (lineage-22.2, srcs IAllocator.hal, interfaces common@1.0
// + mapper@2.0 + hidl.base@1.0, gen_java false).
// hardware/interfaces IS synced, but the closure prune keeps
// ONLY light/aidl + compatibility_matrices + common/aidl +
// input/common/aidl, so allocator/2.0 is pruned - same story
// as mapper@4.0 (#105). Used in shared_libs by
// libgrallocusage (system/core/libgrallocusage/Android.bp:44,
// verified in the manifest-pinned tree) and by libs/ui +
// surfaceflinger. Stubbed plain cc_library (both variants;
// the #105 mapper@4.0 shared-only precedent is narrower
// than the subset-reporting lesson allows).
// libstatspull_headers is cc_library_headers in
// packages/modules/StatsD/lib/libstatspull/Android.bp (r32,
// line 80, export_include_dirs ["include"]) -
// packages/modules/StatsD is NOT synced; used in header_libs
// (+ export_header_lib_headers) by libstatspull_lazy
// (system/core/libstats/pull_lazy/Android.bp:11/15).
// libstatssocket_headers is cc_library_headers in
// packages/modules/StatsD/lib/libstatssocket/Android.bp
// (r32, line 87, export_include_dirs ["include"], apex
// com.android.resolv + platform, min_sdk_version 29) - same
// project, NOT synced; used in header_libs (+
// export_header_lib_headers) by libstatspull_lazy (:12) and
// libstatssocket_lazy
// (system/core/libstats/socket_lazy/Android.bp:17/20) and in
// header_libs by libstats push_compat (:41/:56).
// vulkan_headers is cc_library_headers in
// external/vulkan-headers/Android.bp (r32, lines 71-84,
// export_include_dirs ["include"], host_supported,
// vendor_available, sdk_version 24, llndk_headers true) -
// external/vulkan-headers is NOT synced; used in header_libs
// (+ export_header_lib_headers) by libvkjson_ndk
// (frameworks/native/vulkan/vkjson/Android.bp:64) and
// libvkprofiles_ndk (:64) and by libvulkan + nulldrv. NOTE:
// the synced frameworks/native/vulkan/Android.bp defines
// only hwvulkan_headers (the libhardware HAL headers) - a
// DIFFERENT module; Soong's "Or did you mean
// hwvulkan_headers?" suggestion is a red herring.
// libjsoncpp_ndk is cc_library_static in
// external/jsoncpp/Android.bp (r32, lines 85-90, defaults
// libjsoncpp_defaults, sdk_version 9, stl libc++_static) -
// external/jsoncpp is NOT synced; used in whole_static_libs
// by libvkjson_ndk (vkjson/Android.bp:61). Stub mirrors
// upstream: cc_library_static with stl: "libc++_static"
// (device-only module, no windows variant, so no
// libwinpthread-class cycle).
// ndk_system (#156 only): libomp is
// llvm_prebuilt_library_static in
// prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/Android.bp (:48,
// sdk_version "minimum", no stl:). Soong's stl.go makes any
// sdk_version module with no stl: take SelectedStl
// "ndk_system" (useSdk && Device), and the ndk_system STL
// case appends "ndk_system" to HeaderLibs - so the dep is a
// HEADER_LIBS use. The real module is NOT defined anywhere
// in the synced tree (zero mentions in any synced .bp; not
// in bionic/libc or prebuilts/sdk at r32 - home not traced,
// same class as #105 libgtest_isolated/libprocinfo).
// Stubbed cc_library_headers. NOTE: the same STL case also
// appends "libstdc++" to SharedLibs - no stub needed there,
// libstdc++ IS defined in the synced
// bionic/libc/Android.bp (:1947/:2333), which is why it
// never errored.
// COMPILE-STAGE CAVEAT: the four cc_library_headers stubs
// are bare (no export_include_dirs, no real headers), as
// all earlier headers stubs were - a bare stub passes
// Soong; dummy headers will be needed only if the next run
// fails at compile/link because libstatspull_lazy /
// libstatssocket_lazy / libvkjson_ndk / libvkprofiles_ndk
// actually include the headers (same class as the #111
// libgsi / #135 flatbuffer caveats). The allocator@2.0 +
// libjsoncpp_ndk stubs are bare too (empty.c, no symbols);
// the HAL closure never links libgrallocusage /
// libvkjson_ndk / libomp, so those may never surface.
// Runs #159/#160/#161 fix: runs #159 (45939727734, 15m39s,
// auto, manifest 05d7ff1), #160 (45939796587, 14m41s, auto,
// README 22c7771) and #161 (45939833196, 13m01s, manual
// dispatch ~09:55 IST 2026-11-27, head 22c7771 - the runs
// #156/#157/#158 fix, workflow d83cd90) ALL FAILED at
// Soong ninja-file generation, 38-54s into the build step,
// on the SAME fix code. The #156/#157/#158 fix HELD
// COMPLETELY in all three (prune step passed + pre-build
// guard passed; ZERO genuine "depends on undefined module"
// lines in any raw log). NEW failure class - "missing
// variant", exactly ONE genuine error per run, different
// each time (subset variation - the fix covers the UNION).
// All fail at Soong bootstrap [100% 114/114] analyzing,
// FAILED: out/soong/build.yuzora_lights.ninja, soong
// bootstrap failed exit status 1. Raw-log verbatim error
// union (browser job-logs.txt read of all three raw logs;
// the earlier UI report of "android.hardware.lights-
// service.samsung / product m51 / missing and no known
// rule" is a CONFIRMED PHANTOM - it appears nowhere
// genuine in any raw log, same class as #152):
//   error: prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/Android.bp:48:1:
//     dependency "ndk_system" of "libomp" missing variant:
//     (#161) requested variant
//     os:android,arch:arm64_armv8-a,sdk:sdk; available
//     variants os:linux_glibc,arch:x86_64,
//     os:linux_glibc,arch:x86, os:windows,arch:x86,
//     os:windows,arch:x86_64, os:android,arch:arm64_armv8-a.
//   error: prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/Android.bp:337:1:
//     dependency "ndk_system" of "libsimpleperf_readelf"
//     missing variant: (#160) same requested + available
//     variants.
//   error: frameworks/native/vulkan/vkprofiles/Android.bp:44:1:
//     dependency "vulkan_headers" of "libvkprofiles_ndk"
//     missing variant: (#159) same requested + available
//     variants.
// Root cause, verified in the synced Soong source
// (manifest-pinned tree ~/workspace/lights-local/build/
// soong): the bare cc_library_headers stubs resolve as
// modules but only build the PLATFORM variant. The sdk
// transition mutator (cc/sdk.go Split) creates the
// {"sdk", "sdk"} variation ONLY for a module whose
// UseSdk() is true, and UseSdk() (cc/cc.go:1309) is true
// exactly when Sdk_version is set (canUseSdk + non-empty
// sdk_version); without one the module gets only the ""
// (platform) variation. The NDK consumers all set
// sdk_version, so they request the sdk:sdk variant of
// their deps: libomp + libsimpleperf_readelf are
// llvm_prebuilt_library_static with sdk_version "minimum"
// (prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/Android.bp:48/:337,
// verified in the manifest-pinned tree); libvkprofiles_ndk
// + libvkjson_ndk are cc_library_static with sdk_version
// "24" (frameworks/native/vulkan/vkprofiles/Android.bp +
// vkjson/Android.bp, same tree). A bare stub with no
// sdk_version can never satisfy an sdk consumer, however
// many modules are stubbed.
// Fix: NO new stubs, NO new projects (still 32). Three
// sdk_version lines INSERTED into the existing d83cd90
// stub blocks below, so the diff vs d83cd90 is
// additions-only (the lines are insertions, not edits of
// existing lines - justified here because the stub type
// and every other property are unchanged):
//   vulkan_headers: sdk_version: "24" - mirrors upstream
//   r32 (external/vulkan-headers/Android.bp, sdk_version
//   24); both sdk consumers are 24, so the NDK link check
//   (cc/cc.go: an NDK lib must not link a dep built
//   against a NEWER api) passes exactly. "current" would
//   be WRONG: a non-current consumer may not link a
//   "current" dep.
//   ndk_system: sdk_version: "minimum" - there is NO
//   upstream module to mirror (zero mentions in any synced
//   .bp; Soong-internal STL pseudo-dep, build/soong/cc/
//   stl.go:168-173); both consumers are "minimum", and
//   "minimum" is the LOWEST value so every consumer's link
//   check passes ("current" would fail it). Precedent:
//   the ndk_prebuilt STL defaults in the synced
//   prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/Android.bp carry
//   sdk_version "minimum". No self-dependency: stl.go
//   begin() gives a cc_library_headers module SelectedStl
//   "" (ctx.header() -> stl "none"), so the stub does NOT
//   gain an ndk_system dep on itself.
//   libjsoncpp_ndk: sdk_version: "9" - mirrors upstream
//   r32 (external/jsoncpp/Android.bp, sdk_version 9); the
//   provably-next layer, not speculation: libvkjson_ndk
//   (sdk_version 24) takes this stub in whole_static_libs,
//   so it WILL demand the sdk variant on the next run.
//   Its sdk variant's STL deps (ndk_libc++_static +
//   ndk_libc++abi + libunwind, stl.go:175-180) are all
//   defined in the synced prebuilts/clang/host/linux-x86/
//   Android.bp (:509/:515/:521/:315) with sdk variants of
//   their own (sdk_version "minimum" via defaults), so no
//   new undefined-module layer opens; the link check passes
//   (dep 9 < consumer 24).
// NOT changed now, verified with evidence:
// libstatspull_headers + libstatssocket_headers - no sdk
// consumer exists in the closure: libstatspull_lazy +
// libstatssocket_lazy carry no sdk_version (system/core/
// libstats/pull_lazy + socket_lazy/Android.bp),
// libstatspush_compat carries only min_sdk_version "29"
// (push_compat/Android.bp:60), and libinput (the only other
// libstatssocket_lazy consumer) carries no sdk_version.
// android.hardware.graphics.allocator@2.0 - no sdk consumer
// either: libgrallocusage carries only min_sdk_version
// "29", libs/ui only min_sdk_version, surfaceflinger none
// - and min_sdk_version alone does NOT set UseSdk()
// (cc/cc.go:1309 - only Sdk_version does). If a future run
// reports a missing-variant line for any of these three,
// the fix is the same one-line sdk_version addition.
// The prune step + the pre-build guard both verify the
// three sdk_version lines (sed block range, #110-safe).
cc_library {
    name: "android.hardware.graphics.allocator@2.0",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_headers {
    name: "libstatspull_headers",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_headers {
    name: "libstatssocket_headers",
    host_supported: true,
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_headers {
    name: "vulkan_headers",
    host_supported: true,
    // Runs #159/#160/#161 fix: sdk_version "24" (see the
    // comment block above the allocator@2.0 stub). Without
    // it the stub builds only the platform variant, and
    // the sdk_version-24 NDK consumers libvkjson_ndk +
    // libvkprofiles_ndk fail with "missing variant" for
    // the requested sdk:sdk variant.
    sdk_version: "24",
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_static {
    name: "libjsoncpp_ndk",
    srcs: ["empty.c"],
    stl: "libc++_static",
    // Runs #159/#160/#161 fix: sdk_version "9" (see the
    // comment block above the allocator@2.0 stub). The
    // provably-next layer: libvkjson_ndk (sdk_version 24)
    // takes this stub in whole_static_libs, so it will
    // demand the sdk variant on the next run.
    sdk_version: "9",
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
cc_library_headers {
    name: "ndk_system",
    host_supported: true,
    // Runs #159/#160/#161 fix: sdk_version "minimum"
    // (see the comment block above the allocator@2.0
    // stub). Without it the stub builds only the platform
    // variant, and the sdk_version-"minimum" consumers
    // libomp + libsimpleperf_readelf fail with "missing
    // variant" for the requested sdk:sdk variant.
    sdk_version: "minimum",
    visibility: [
        "//visibility:public",
    ],
}
// Runs #165/#166/#167 fix: eleven new stubs (see the
// comment block in the prune step above for the per-module
// verification). librustutils is a rust_library (crate_name
// "rustutils", srcs lib.rs — reused from the #96 libcxx
// stub, same form as the #116 rust stubs). The eight plain
// cc_library stubs mirror the libstatspull form (srcs
// empty.c, host_supported, windows target, public): a plain
// cc_library yields both variants, so one stub satisfies
// shared_libs and static_libs consumers alike. The two
// bpf headers stubs mirror the libstatspull_headers form
